course: dictionary
lesson: 982
title: Boastful and showing off
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Boastful means talking too proudly about yourself, your skills or your things, so that other people feel you are showing off. A boastful person wants everyone to notice how good they are.
explain: Look for the clues in this sentence: «Nobody likes a boastful winner.» The winner is talking loudly about winning, and that is why people do not like it. Winning is fine. Bragging about it is the problem.
explain: Boastful often appears in stories about character. In «The Tortoise and the Hare», the hare is boastful, so sure he will win that he is careless. To check your meaning, swap in your own idea of "showing off" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Boastful is an adjective, so it can change: boastful, more boastful, most boastful.
fact: «Boastful» means talking too proudly about yourself, your skills or your things.
fact: «Conceited» means thinking too much of yourself; «boastful» means always showing off about what you have or do.
fact: Phrases to know: «boastful about» something, and «boastful talk».
fact: The hare in «The Tortoise and the Hare» is a famous boastful character.
exercise: «Nobody likes a boastful winner.» What does boastful mean here? | Tired after running a long way | *Talking too proudly about winning, so others feel you are showing off | Shy and quiet after a race | Happy to share the prize with everyone
exercise: Ravi says, «He is always boastful about his new bike.» Which meaning fits best? | Sad because he has lost his bike | Shy about his new bike | *Always talking proudly about his bike so others notice | Hungry for a long bike ride
exercise: Which word describes someone who thinks too much of himself? | Ancient | *Conceited | Curious | Glum
test: In «The Tortoise and the Hare», the hare is boastful. What does this tell us about him? | *He talks too proudly about how fast he is | He is very old and wise | He is quiet and humble about his speed | He never runs at all
test: Which phrase means talk that shows off? | Kind talk | Slow talk | Quiet talk | *Boastful talk
exam: Read this: «He's kind and good-natured, though perhaps not very clever, and rather boastful and conceited.» What does boastful suggest about him? | He is quiet and shy about his successes | *He shows off and talks too proudly about himself | He is always sad | He is very clever and never makes mistakes
